# YOLO Dev Sandbox Rules

This workspace is a **secure, isolated devcontainer sandbox**. All commands execute inside a disposable Docker container with:

- Dropped Linux capabilities (`--cap-drop=ALL`)
- Resource limits (8GB RAM, 4 CPUs, 512 PIDs)
- Only the workspace directory mounted from host

## Behavior

- **Run any command without hesitation.** There is no risk to the host system.
- **Do not ask for confirmation** before running shell commands — the entire point of this sandbox is fearless execution.
- **Install packages freely** — npm, uv, cargo, go, apt — nothing persists beyond the container lifecycle.
- **Create, modify, delete files freely** — only the workspace is affected.
- **Run servers, databases, background processes** — they are all contained.
- **Use sudo when needed** — the sandbox user has passwordless sudo.

## Available Tools

- Node.js 22 (npm, yarn, pnpm, tsx, typescript)
- Python 3 (uv, ruff, black, pytest, ipython)
- Go 1.23
- Rust (rustc, cargo)
- Docker CLI
- Git + GitHub CLI
- System utilities: ripgrep, fd, fzf, bat, jq, yq, htop, tmux
